Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Restore the TEB GSBASE in sigsys_handler on macOS.

init_handler() switches GSBASE to the pthread TSD, but unlike the other
handlers sigsys_handler() never calls leave_handler(), so it returns into
__wine_syscall_dispatcher with GSBASE still pointing at the pthread TSD.
The dispatcher reads %gs:0x30 as the TEB, gets NULL and faults, and the
direct syscall fails with STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION.

Seen with games whose protection issues raw syscalls (Age of Empires II/III
Definitive Edition, NtAllocateVirtualMemory, SSN 0x18).
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
index 7bff70b..72eb861 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -2608,6 +2608,10 @@ static void sigsys_handler( int signal, siginfo_t *siginfo, void *_sigcontext )
         frame->restore_flags |= CONTEXT_CONTROL;
     }
     RIP_sig(sigcontext) = (ULONG64)__wine_syscall_dispatcher_prolog_end_ptr;
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+    /* init_handler() switched GSBASE to the pthread TSD; the dispatcher expects the TEB. */
+    _thread_set_tsd_base( (uint64_t)data->teb );
+#endif
 }
 #endif
 
